{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a1-day-kids-netherlands/audio/main-b0da9a176fcf.mp3","durationSec":200.4,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.68,"text":"It is seven o'clock."},{"start":1.68,"end":3.36,"text":"The children get up and go to the kitchen."},{"start":4,"end":4.78,"text":"Breakfast is bread."},{"start":5.66,"end":6.84,"text":"On the bread, there is butter."},{"start":7.62,"end":9.14,"text":"On the butter, there is hagelslag."},{"start":9.9,"end":12,"text":"Hagelslag is very small pieces of chocolate."},{"start":12.62,"end":14.54,"text":"The butter helps the chocolate stay on the bread."},{"start":14.54,"end":16.52,"text":"Dutch children love it!"},{"start":17.08,"end":19.16,"text":"On other days, they eat cheese on their bread."},{"start":19.74,"end":20.2,"text":"Why bread?"},{"start":20.94,"end":24.02,"text":"Dutch people often eat bread in the morning and again at lunch."},{"start":24.7,"end":26.16,"text":"The hot food comes in the evening."},{"start":27.12,"end":29.22,"text":"Many Dutch children go to school by bike."},{"start":29.22,"end":29.98,"text":"Why?"},{"start":30.82,"end":32.98,"text":"Most of the country is flat, like a table."},{"start":32.98,"end":36.1,"text":"There are not many big hills, so riding is easy."},{"start":36.82,"end":39.66,"text":"Many streets also have a special place only for bikes."},{"start":39.66,"end":42.32,"text":"Small children ride with Mom or Dad."},{"start":42.98,"end":44.06,"text":"Big children ride alone."},{"start":44.96,"end":47.36,"text":"At about ten years old, children take a bike test."},{"start":48.04,"end":50.58,"text":"They ride on real streets, and people watch them."},{"start":51.24,"end":51.8,"text":"Why a test?"},{"start":52.58,"end":55.26,"text":"There are cars on the street, so children must ride well."},{"start":55.66,"end":57.28,"text":"School starts at half past eight."},{"start":57.28,"end":59.5,"text":"Children bring a lunch box from home."},{"start":60.22,"end":63,"text":"In the box, there is bread again, maybe with cheese."},{"start":63.74,"end":64.36,"text":"Why from home?"},{"start":64.82,"end":66.8,"text":"Most Dutch schools do not cook lunch."},{"start":67.3,"end":69.28,"text":"The children eat in the classroom with their teacher."},{"start":69.68,"end":70.52,"text":"Then they play outside."},{"start":71.26,"end":74.16,"text":"In Japan, the school gives children a hot lunch."},{"start":75.26,"end":76.52,"text":"Birthdays are fun at school."},{"start":77.02,"end":79.5,"text":"The birthday child brings something small to eat."},{"start":80.02,"end":81.72,"text":"It is for all the children in the class."},{"start":82.4,"end":83.44,"text":"It is often fruit."},{"start":84.26,"end":85.82,"text":"Why does the birthday child give food?"},{"start":86.24,"end":89.24,"text":"In the Netherlands, on your birthday, you give to other people."},{"start":89.62,"end":90.44,"text":"You do not only get."},{"start":91.52,"end":94,"text":"After school, children play outside with friends."},{"start":94.6,"end":96.28,"text":"They also go to swimming lessons."},{"start":97.06,"end":97.24,"text":"Why?"},{"start":97.84,"end":101.56,"text":"The Netherlands has water everywhere: rivers, canals and the sea."},{"start":102.18,"end":104.54,"text":"A canal is a long river made by people."},{"start":105.2,"end":107.66,"text":"Near all this water, children must swim well."},{"start":108.02,"end":111.02,"text":"For the first swimming test, children swim in their clothes and shoes."},{"start":111.64,"end":112.14,"text":"Why clothes?"},{"start":112.68,"end":115.54,"text":"Sometimes a child goes into the water with clothes on."},{"start":116.28,"end":117.7,"text":"Then the child must swim in clothes!"},{"start":118.42,"end":120.66,"text":"In a very cold winter, the water turns to ice."},{"start":121.48,"end":123.7,"text":"Then families go on the ice with special shoes."},{"start":124.16,"end":125,"text":"This is ice skating."},{"start":125.64,"end":126.4,"text":"Children love it."},{"start":127.3,"end":129.44,"text":"Dinner is early, at about six o'clock."},{"start":129.44,"end":131.46,"text":"The family sits at the table and eats together."},{"start":132.12,"end":135.08,"text":"Now the food is hot: potatoes, vegetables and meat."},{"start":135.68,"end":136.3,"text":"Why so early?"},{"start":137.16,"end":139.56,"text":"After dinner, the family has more time together."},{"start":140.22,"end":142.04,"text":"Then the children brush their teeth."},{"start":142.82,"end":144.04,"text":"They read a book and go to bed."},{"start":144.04,"end":147.1,"text":"In November, Sinterklaas comes to the Netherlands."},{"start":147.7,"end":149.44,"text":"He is an old man with a long white beard."},{"start":149.92,"end":150.96,"text":"He wears red clothes."},{"start":151.78,"end":154.42,"text":"In the story, he comes from Spain on a big boat."},{"start":154.86,"end":155.88,"text":"He rides a white horse."},{"start":156.82,"end":159.66,"text":"At night, children put one shoe near the fire or the window."},{"start":160.08,"end":161.98,"text":"They put a carrot in the shoe for the horse."},{"start":162.7,"end":162.9,"text":"Why?"},{"start":163.62,"end":166.64,"text":"In the story, the horse runs over the houses all night."},{"start":167.18,"end":167.9,"text":"It gets hungry!"},{"start":168.42,"end":170.5,"text":"In the morning, the carrot is gone."},{"start":171.22,"end":173.86,"text":"In the shoe, there are sweets or a small present."},{"start":174.6,"end":177.22,"text":"On 5 December, children get their big presents."},{"start":179.36,"end":182.2,"text":"On 27 April, it is King's Day."},{"start":182.82,"end":183.96,"text":"It is the king's birthday."},{"start":184.66,"end":185.92,"text":"Everyone wears orange."},{"start":186.74,"end":187.42,"text":"Why orange?"},{"start":188.18,"end":190.14,"text":"The king's family has the name Orange."},{"start":191.14,"end":193.56,"text":"Children sell their old toys on the street."},{"start":194.34,"end":196.84,"text":"On other days, people must ask the town first."},{"start":197.38,"end":199.78,"text":"On King's Day, they do not need to ask!"}],"words":[{"text":"It","start":0,"end":0.14},{"text":"is","start":0.14,"end":0.28},{"text":"seven","start":0.28,"end":0.6},{"text":"o'clock","start":0.6,"end":1.68},{"text":"The","start":1.68,"end":1.7},{"text":"children","start":1.7,"end":1.94},{"text":"get","start":1.94,"end":2.24},{"text":"up","start":2.24,"end":2.44},{"text":"and","start":2.44,"end":2.68},{"text":"go","start":2.68,"end":2.84},{"text":"to","start":2.84,"end":2.94},{"text":"the","start":2.94,"end":3.04},{"text":"kitchen","start":3.04,"end":3.36},{"text":"Breakfast","start":4,"end":4.2},{"text":"is","start":4.2,"end":4.5},{"text":"bread","start":4.5,"end":4.78},{"text":"On","start":5.66,"end":5.74},{"text":"the","start":5.74,"end":5.88},{"text":"bread","start":5.88,"end":6.12},{"text":"there","start":6.36,"end":6.42},{"text":"is","start":6.42,"end":6.58},{"text":"butter","start":6.58,"end":6.84},{"text":"On","start":7.62,"end":7.72},{"text":"the","start":7.72,"end":7.84},{"text":"butter","start":7.84,"end":8.1},{"text":"there","start":8.34,"end":8.42},{"text":"is","start":8.42,"end":8.6},{"text":"hagelslag","start":8.6,"end":9.14},{"text":"Hagelslag","start":9.9,"end":10.34},{"text":"is","start":10.34,"end":10.58},{"text":"very","start":10.58,"end":10.82},{"text":"small","start":10.82,"end":11.16},{"text":"pieces","start":11.16,"end":11.44},{"text":"of","start":11.44,"end":11.68},{"text":"chocolate","start":11.68,"end":12},{"text":"The","start":12.62,"end":12.76},{"text":"butter","start":12.76,"end":12.96},{"text":"helps","start":12.96,"end":13.2},{"text":"the","start":13.2,"end":13.4},{"text":"chocolate","start":13.4,"end":13.74},{"text":"stay","start":13.74,"end":14.04},{"text":"on","start":14.04,"end":14.2},{"text":"the","start":14.2,"end":14.32},{"text":"bread","start":14.32,"end":14.54},{"text":"Dutch","start":14.54,"end":15.58},{"text":"chil